From 6b484ced23955306d6c63ec6afa0cb10bf933c7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:10:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep queued data when the login is lost (audit 2-B)

A 401 used to be treated like any other 4xx: the outbox dropped the
item, so every answer after a mid-practice logout vanished silently.
Now the outbox keeps the item, stops, and the nav sends the child back
to the picker with an explanation; once they pick their name again the
queue is resent unchanged (opId prevents double counting). Telemetry
and battle reports keep their data on 401 the same way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WUbHSQPhe2C6SfdgHzcHBA
